[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4964909767","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121338#issuecomment-4964909767","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121338","id":4964909767,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJ-6Cxw","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-14T02:46:06Z","updated_at":"2026-07-14T02:46:06Z","body":"@kitbdev @AdriaandeJongh Apologies for the ping, but your re-review and approvals would be appreciated! The contents of the commit for this PR should be identical to the last one pushed for #114168 (hash must be different since it has a different parent commit?). With your approvals as well as one from the GDScript team, it sounds like this should be good to merge 😄 ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4964909767/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5040149328","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121338#issuecomment-5040149328","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121338","id":5040149328,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLGqTUA","user":{"login":"kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev","html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-21T23:35:11Z","updated_at":"2026-07-21T23:35:11Z","body":"@YeldhamDev Note that this still needs a GDScript review, it is not ready to merge yet. It was already reverted once for not having it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5040149328/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5054723456","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121338#issuecomment-5054723456","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121338","id":5054723456,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLUj1gA","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-23T05:12:50Z","updated_at":"2026-07-23T05:12:50Z","body":"I've now cleaned up the code in `gdscript_analyzer.cpp` so that the `TOOLS_ENABLED` blocks are much smaller and simpler; the code action-building logic now lives in its own file and namespace, `GDScriptCodeActions`, which the analyzer simply calls methods from to build the sets of code actions for particular warnings.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5054723456/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5386768745","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121338#issuecomment-5386768745","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121338","id":5386768745,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQRORaQ","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-23T15:23:54Z","updated_at":"2026-08-23T15:25:52Z","body":"Pushed a tiny fix for a bug that was causing quick fixes to only be available when the caret was on the starting line of a warning or an error. Now, multi-line warnings and errors will display the quick fix button when the caret is on any of their lines.\r\n\r\n_Edit: Actually amending the bug-fixing changes to the commit before pushing helps fix the bugs!_","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5386768745/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5418180826","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121338#issuecomment-5418180826","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121338","id":5418180826,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQvLg2g","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-25T23:12:39Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T23:12:39Z","body":"With more code being moved into `EditorLanguage`, and this being an editor-specific feature that's also tied closely to the compiler/analyzer, the implementation is getting trickier 😅\r\nMy initial plan today, and what I implemented with my latest commit, was to use a different function signature for `push_warning` and `push_error` depending on if `TOOLS_ENABLED` was defined. (Specifically, when it is defined the methods take an extra argument for a list of code actions to associate with the diagnostic.)\r\n\r\nHowever, I'm not happy with how this looks in the analyzer. In the most frustrating cases, it can take a line like:\r\n```cpp\r\nparser->push_warning(p_assignable, GDScriptWarning::INFERENCE_ON_VARIANT, {}, p_kind);\r\n```\r\nand require it to become:\r\n```cpp\r\n#ifdef TOOLS_ENABLED\r\nparser->push_warning(p_assignable, GDScriptWarning::INFERENCE_ON_VARIANT, {}, p_kind);\r\n#else\r\nparser->push_warning(p_assignable, GDScriptWarning::INFERENCE_ON_VARIANT, p_kind);\r\n#endif // TOOLS_ENABLED\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhile working on this, I came up with an idea for an alternative approach where the `push_warning()` signature is unchanged, but inside of `push_warning()`, when `TOOLS_ENABLED` is defined we use AST node information passed in to generate the code actions. Depending on the info available from the nodes, it's possible we may need to still change the signature so we can pass in necessary extra data that the code action generation uses.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5418180826/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5421069369","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121338#issuecomment-5421069369","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121338","id":5421069369,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQx70OQ","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-26T05:35:32Z","updated_at":"2026-08-26T05:35:32Z","body":"Very good happy news! The alternative approach I was thinking of as I completed the previous work, I went ahead and implemented. Now the analyzer and compiler have _minimal_ changes, and the code action-building code is now isolated in the `gdscript_code_actions.h` file 😄 \r\n\r\nAs I've been working on _all of this today_, I've also been coming to the increasingly strong conclusion that it'd be good to add a system for running tests to this, similar to the autocompletion testing system. It'd probably be good to have alongside this first implementation of the system, but I'll probably work on it on a separate branch at first.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5421069369/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":2,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5430828420","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121338#issuecomment-5430828420","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121338","id":5430828420,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQ7PdhA","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-26T20:38:24Z","updated_at":"2026-08-26T20:38:24Z","body":"More very good happy news! I spent this morning using the autocompletion unit test system as a basis for making a code action unit test system. So now we can very easily write tests to verify that code actions/quick fixes are working properly!\r\n\r\nIn the process of doing this, I came to the realization that the \"Call from type\" quick fix for STATIC_CALLED_ON_INSTANCE was not working properly, so for now I made the decision to remove it. From looking over the analyzer code, it seems that maybe it requires some information that the node passed to `push_warning` itself doesn't have access to. With the new approach to code actions that minimizes impact on the analyzer, there's no longer a way (at least that I could discern) to get that info.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5430828420/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5705192222","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121338#issuecomment-5705192222","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121338","id":5705192222,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABVA5THg","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-16T22:00:46Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T22:00:46Z","body":"Thanks for the feedback and questions, both here and on the RocketChat! I've just gone through and updated the PR.\r\n\r\nLooking over the feedback, these are the big changes I made in response:\r\n- Started using the existing `EditorLanguage::TextEdit` and got rid of this PR's `ScriptLanguage::TextEdit`\r\n- Removed unnecessary `#include` in `editor_settings.cpp`\r\n- Removed redundant `#ifdef TOOLS_ENABLED` blocks\r\n- Removed `to_dict()` and `from_dict()` methods from classes/structs in `EditorLanguage`, and migrated that code to the editor side where it is used\r\n- Removed `get_code_actions()` and started using the output from `validate()` instead\r\n- Added documentation comments to new structs in `EditorLanguage` to (try to) explain how/why they work, and what the overall structure of a `CodeActionGroup` is\r\n  - Please let me know if it's still confusing and I can try to do a dedicated write-up about it! \r\n- Removed `CodeActionGroupAndDiagnostics` and related structs, to keep things simple(r)\r\n- Moved most instances of `Vector` to `LocalVector` since COW isn't necessary\r\n- Updated the test system to work with the aforementioned structural changes","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5705192222/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5708369381","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121338#issuecomment-5708369381","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121338","id":5708369381,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABVD7N5Q","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-17T04:13:12Z","updated_at":"2026-09-17T04:13:12Z","body":"Code actions for warnings treated as errors are now supported again!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5708369381/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6160996494","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121338#issuecomment-6160996494","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121338","id":6160996494,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABbzlYjg","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-14T04:36:40Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T03:30:26Z","body":"While working on #124417, I realized that it would be much easier to get information about the node tree for use in code actions if I let the analyzer finish running before creating the code actions, instead of attempting to create them as soon as a warning or error that warrants them is detected.\r\n\r\nIn the next couple of days, I may see if I can go through this PR's code and tweak it a bit to use this \"queueing\" approach.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe new queueing approach has been implemented!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6160996494/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6198271027","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121338#issuecomment-6198271027","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121338","id":6198271027,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABcXIcMw","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-15T17:32:25Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T17:32:25Z","body":"Today I fixed bugs where trying to eliminate a multi-line variable or constant declaration would only delete its first line, instead of the entire thing. I also improved the placement of the quick fix icon popup location.\r\n\r\nI did note that when there is no space on either the current or adjacent lines, the quick fix button gets overlaid on the current line's text, which is not great:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"332\" height=\"125\" alt=\"CleanShot 2026-10-15 at 10 00 24 AM@2x\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/04f64f84-2093-4896-bec5-925c99e0a3a5\" />\r\n\r\nAs I recall, VS Code's solution in this case is to place it in the gutter, possibly over the top of the line number. Does this sound like a good approach, or does anyone have other ideas for things to try here?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6198271027/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]